.TH DTDSPMSG 1 "2026-11-22" "Amiga UNIX add-on" "CDE"
.SH NAME
dtdspmsg \- print a message from a message catalogue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtdspmsg
.RB [ \-s
.IR set ]
.I catalogue
.I number
.RI [ default
.RI [ argument " ...]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dtdspmsg
prints message
.I number
of
.I set
(default 1) from the message catalogue
.IR catalogue ,
found through
.B NLSPATH
as
.BR catopen (3C)
finds it, with the
.IR argument s
put in for its conversions
.RB ( %s ,
or
.BI % n \e
for the
.IR n th).
When the catalogue or the message is not found it prints
.I default
instead, with the escapes
.BR \en ,
.BR \et ,
.BR \eb ,
.BR \er ,
.BR \ev ,
.BR \ef ,
.BI \ex hh
and octal
.BI \e ooo
in it expanded.
Shell scripts of the desktop use it to print their messages in the
user's language.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 12
.B NLSPATH
where the catalogues are looked for
.TP
.B LANG
the language
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gencat (1),
.BR catgets (3C)
